    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABIibqOA",
      "title": "agents: Add specification consistency reviewer",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 972,
      "body": "Add a repository-local consistency reviewer for specification reviews. The reviewer checks for conflicting requirements, stale statements, incomplete exhaustive lists, and differences between prose and pseudocode. It traces related sections beyond the changed lines and requires evidence for each finding.\n\nThe reviewer treats explicit hard fork changes as expected behavior, not contradictions. It checks scope, activation conditions, and amendments before it reports a conflict. Each finding identifies both source locations and explains why the statements cannot both apply.\n\nThe agent uses `model: inherit` and inherits available tools. Its instructions limit it to review without edits and exclude style, implementation quality, and protocol design reviews.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-15T03:55:21Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-04T01:00:15Z",
      "additions": 84,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABMkL4bw",
      "title": "fix: Align delay semantics with `OptimismPortal`, `ASR` and `DelayedWETH` behavior",
      "author": "0xarktos",
      "number": 984,
      "body": "- OptimismPortal: proof maturity check is strict, a withdrawal must be proven more than `proofMaturityDelaySeconds` ago\n- DelayedWETH: `withdraw` reverts if `delay()` is 0\n- AnchorStateRegistry: `isGameFinalized` returns false if `disputeGameFinalityDelaySeconds` is 0",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-03T13:40:16Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-04T21:13:54Z",
      "additions": 11,
      "deletions": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABM61Dzw",
      "title": "interop: Fix the ETHLiquidity initial balance",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 985,
      "body": "The ETHLiquidity spec and the SuperchainETHBridge assumptions said that ETHLiquidity starts with `type(uint248).max` wei. The Lagoon activation deposit mints `type(uint128).max` wei. That is the largest value the deposit `mint` field can hold. op-node and kona both use this value, and `derivation.md` already states it.\n\nThis PR changes `eth-liquidity.md` and `superchain-eth-bridge.md` to `type(uint128).max`. The `type(uint248).max` in the custom gas token spec is for `NativeAssetLiquidity` and is correct.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-04T21:32:44Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-11-04T21:55:01Z",
      "additions": 4,
      "deletions": 4
    }
  ],
